{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Finally, the churches were the subject of conversation. The churches, as I said—in Ghent and Antwerp, one must go there if one wishes to see sublime, rich Catholic churches—large, spacious, Gothic, majestic—stained glass windows (the most beautiful I have ever seen are in Brussels); on the columns, marble statues life-sized, placed at some height, otherwise lying or sitting—in the dozens;—paintings by Rubens, van Dyck, and their pupils, large works, wonderful ones among them, two to three dozen in a single church; marble columns, bas-reliefs, grilles, confessionals, half a dozen or a full dozen in the Antwerp church—each adorned with four life-sized, excellent wood-carved images—(I thought of the English greeting in Nuremberg);—the town halls equally peculiarly Gothic. We were on our feet in Antwerp for four hours in the morning;—I have sweated a lot for the past eight days; at Waterloo I thought that it had not been quite as much as the French and the Allies had sweated. In Antwerp I parted from my dear friend Mr. van Ghert; he went back to Brussels with the instruction to inquire whether any letters from you had arrived, and to send them to me in Amsterdam."}}],"created":1795218865,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":270,"prompt_tokens":393,"total_tokens":663,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-yIOVOPAyZUhEmfRgsclXtuh5q9KMGsc7","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":393,"prompt_ms":484.179,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.232007633587786,"prompt_per_second":811.6832824224099,"predicted_n":270,"predicted_ms":6376.577,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.70474721189591,"predicted_per_second":42.185642861365906}}